DIR [v:][pattern] [FULL]
  A drive's files across the screen. pattern: * any characters, ? any one
  (*.CYB, T*). B alone: drive B. FULL: a line each, with its size.
  With UniDOS the folder itself (folders shown NAME/):
  DIR IDE:            DIR SD:GAMES/*.BAS      DIR GAMES/
  FULL then: sizes, dates; hidden files too.
  A RAM disc (Z, RAMDISC's): its own directory. A floppy AMSDOS runs:
  FLOPPY A lists it.
